{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And Moses chose able men.</b> After he sought and did not find men who possessed all the qualities that Jethro had mentioned, he chose able men — expert and diligent men — to examine and clarify the truths of a matter and bring it to its proper end, in preference over God-fearing men who are not able men. As the Sages, of blessed memory, said (Shabbat 63a): 'If a scholar is like a snake, gird him about your loins; and if an ignoramus is pious, do not dwell in his neighborhood.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:26:10.151175649Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}